    "ls|LS16_S12_U_272": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 272 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18TH JULY, 2017 \n \nIMPORT OF WHEAT \n272.  DR. P. VENUGOPAL: \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC \nDISTRIBUTION miHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h   be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is not  considering to import wheat on  \nGovernment account;  \n \n(b) whether the country has enough wheat to meet the requirement under the  \nPublic Distribution System;  \n \n(c) whether it is true that as on December 1, 2016 Food Corporation of  India \nhad 27.55 million tonne of foodgrains  out of which the quantum of wheat was  \n16.4 million tonne and rice was 11 million tonne; and \n \n(d) whether the Government is encouraging import of wheat by private players \nby scrapping import duty on wheat and if so, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR  CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI C. R. CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a):  Yes Madam, there is no proposal to      import wheat on Government \nAccount. \n \n(b): Stock of wheat in the Central Pool as on 1\nst July, 2017 was 32.275 \nmillion tonne against stock norms of 27.58 million tonne as on 1 st July which \nis adequate to meet the requirement under Public Distribution System. \n \n(c): The stock of foodgrains as on 1\nst December, 2016 was 27.555 million \ntonne of which the quantum of wheat was 16.496 million tonne and rice was \n11.059 million tonne.     \n \n(d): The Import duty on wheat has been imposed @ 10% vide notification \ndated 28\nth March, 2017. \n \n**** \n \n \n\n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_273": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES,\nRIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*273\nANSWERED ON 03.08.2017\nRE-LINING OF RAJASTHAN FEEDER CANAL\n†*273. SHRI ARJUN LAL MEENA\nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA\nREJUVENATION be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the NITI Aayog/Union Government has granted approval for investment in re -lining of\nRajasthan feeder canal (Punjab Region) on which the work w ill be carried out by the State\nGovernment of Punjab and if so, the details thereof;\n(b) whether the Union Government has released the funds as sought by the State Government of\nPunjab and if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether the work on the said proj ect has started and if so, the details and the present status\nthereof; and\n(d) if not, the time frame set for implementation of the said project?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER FOR WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA\nREJUVENATION\n(SUSHRI UMA BHARTI)\n(a) to (d)    A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n*****\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED IN REPLY TO PART s (A) TO (D ) OF STARRED QUESTION\nNO. †*273 TO BE ANSWERED ON 03.08.2017 IN LOK SABHA REGARDING “RE -\nLINING OF RAJASTHAN FEEDER CANAL” ASKED BY SHRI ARJUN LAL MEENA:\n(a) The investment clearance for the revised cost of Rs.1305.267 crore of Rajasthan Feeder Canal\n(Punjab Part) has been given on 6th April, 2016.\n(b) Under Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojana (PMKSY), ninety nine (99) ongoing projects\n(along with phases) having irrigation potential of 76.03 lakh ha. have been identified in\nconsultation with States for completion in phases up to December, 2019. Rajasthan feeder canal is\nnot part of these projects. The funding of Rajasthan feeder canal depends upon availability of funds\nand requisite approvals.\n(c) & (d) As intimated by the concerned states, the work for Rajasthan feeder canal has not started.\nFurther, they have indicated that implementation period of the project is 3 years.\n*****",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_274": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*274 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.08.2017 \n \nSports Academy \n \n†*274. DR. MANOJ RAJORIA: \n \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a) whether the Government provides funds to various States to set up \nsports academy in their States;  \n(b) if so, the details along with the funds allocated for the purpose \nduring each of the last three years and the current year, State/UT -wise \nincluding Rajasthan;  \n(c) whether any proposal from the State of Rajasthan to set up sports \nacademy is pending with the Government; and  \n(d) if so, the details and the present status thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a) to (d) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. †*274 FOR 03.08.2017 ASKED BY DR. \nMANOJ RAJORIA, MP, REGARDING SPORTS ACADEMY \n \n(a) & (b) National Sports Academy Scheme is being implemented by \nSports Authority of India (SAI) of this Ministry. U nder this Scheme, no \nfunds have been provided to any State to set up state level academies. \n However, SAI has started some Sports Academies under \ncollaboration with State Governments as under :- \ni) SAI-Odisha Regional Badminton Academy, Bhubaneswar. \nii) SAI National Boxing Academy, Haryana. \niii) SAI National Golf Academy, Trivandrum.  \n \n(c) & (d) No proposal has been received from the State of Rajasthan \nto set up National Sports Academy.  \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_275": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  *275 (15 th  Position)  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03-08-2017 \n \n \nVillages Declared as ODF \n \n*275. SHRIMATI RANJEET RANJAN: \nSHRI VINCENT H. PALA: \n \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of villages declared as Open Defecation Free (ODF) after Ist and 2nd verifications \nby the respective State Governments, out of 2,04,245 villages  which were self-declared by Gram \nPanchayats as ODF as on 23.06.2017, State/UT-wise; \n \n(b) whether the Government is regularly paying the 'commi tment fee' of 0.5% on World Bank loan \nfrom the day of the signing of the agreement in 2015 under Swachh Bharat Mission (SBM); \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof including the total amount of fee paid by the Government till date; \n \n(d) whether the Government has appointed the third party surveying/ monitoring agency for the \nSBM and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(e) if not, the manner in which the Government proposes  to successfully apply for the second \ntranche of the World Bank loan amounting to US $229 million? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n \n \n(a) to (e) A Statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.  *275 for 03.08.2017 \n \n \n(a) A statement regarding State/UT-wise, Open Defecat ion Free (ODF) declared and ODF verified \nvillages by the respective State Governments, as on 23.06.2017 is at Annexure-1. \n \n(b) to (e) The loan agreement for Swachh Bharat Missi on Support Operation was signed between \nWorld Bank and the Government of India on 30th March, 2016. \nThe total World Bank credit obtained for the Project is  US $ 1500 million of which US $ 1475  \nmillion is for providing incentivisation to States on th e basis of their performance as per certain \nperformance indicators known as Disbursement Linked Indi cators (DLIs) and US$ 25 million for \nstrengthening the Programme Management and Capacity Build ing at National Level in MDWS \nthrough an Investment Project Financing (IPF). The commit ment charge payable by the \nGovernment has been fixed to be a quarter of one percent  (0.25%) per annum on the unwithdrawn \nloan balance. \nAs part of the World Bank Project, an Independent Verif ication Agency (IVA) has been appointed \nto conduct National Annual Rural Sanitation Survey (NARSS)  which shall measure and provide \nstatistically representative estimates for progress  made by all States/UTs against the three DLIs. \nThe first and base round of survey is to be scheduled to start from the month of September/October. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure-1. \nStatement referred in part (a) of the reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.275 due for reply on \n03-08-2017 \nState/UT-wise, Total ODF declared and verified villages \n    S.N.  State/UT  ODF declared \nvillages \nODF verified \nvillages \n% ODF \nverified villages \n1 A & N Islands  3 0 0.00  \n2 Andhra Pradesh  4418  1550  35.08  \n3 Arunachal Pradesh  2613  0 0.00  \n4 Assam  1631  164  10.06  \n5 Bihar  2208  63  2.85  \n6 Chhat tisgarh  12832  8526  66.44  \n7 D & N Haveli  0 0 0.00  \n8 Daman & Diu  0 0 0.00  \n9 Goa  0 0 0.00  \n10  Gujarat  15842  14647  92.46  \n11  Haryana  6896  5989  86.85  \n12  Himachal Pradesh  15978  15978  100.00  \n13  Jammu & Kashmir  180  3 1.67  \n14  Jharkhand  5238  1020  19.47  \n15  Kar nataka  7909  2383  30.13  \n16  Kerala  2035  2033  99.90  \n17  Madhya Pradesh  16558  1780  10.75  \n18  Maharashtra  24030  11024  45.88  \n19  Manipur  175  61  34.86  \n20  Meghalaya  3778  2405  63.66  \n21  Mizoram  217  175  80.65  \n22  Nagaland  424  302  71.23  \n23  Odisha  4875  258  5.29  \n24  Puducherry  0 0 0.00  \n25  Punjab  5203  945  18.16  \n26  Rajasthan  20041  10311  51.45  \n27  Sikkim  441  441  100.00  \n28  Tamil Nadu  3699  848  22.93  \n29  Telangana  2020  675  33.42  \n30  Tripura  5 0 0.00  \n31  Uttar Pradesh  7785  936  12.02  \n32  Uttarakhand  15473  9582  61.93  \n33  West Bengal 21738  13357  61.45  \n  Total 204245  105456  51.63  \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_276": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE,\n \nCOOPERATION\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n2\n76\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \nTHE \n18\nTH\n \nJULY\n, \n201\n7\n \n \nPAYMENT OF MSP TO FARMERS\n \n \n276. \n \nADV. NARENDRA KESHAV\n \nS\nAWAIKAR:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n  \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \n \nwhether the Government has asked\n \nall State Governments to ensure that the\n \ndeclared \nMinimum Support Price (MSP)\n \nfor farm produce are paid to the farmers;\n \n \n(b)\n \n \nif so, the details of the States which\n \nha\nve adhered to it; and\n \n \n(c)\n \n \nwhether the Government is\n \nconsidering to extend some financial\n \nassistance to those \nStates which have not\n \npaid MSP to the farmers in order to\n \nsafeguard the interest of the \nfarmers?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF AG\nRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य मं\u0000ी\n \n \n   \n(SHRI S.S. AHLUWALIA)\n \n \n(a) to (c):\n \nThe Government ensures Minimum Support Price (MSP) through procurement \noperations undertaken by the Central, State and Cooperative agencies in the States\n.\n \nState \nGovernme\nnts have been alerted from time to time to \nmake\n \nadequate arrangements to ensure \nMSP to farmers.\n \n \n \nGovernment offers to procure farmers’ produce at MSP, however, they are free to sell it \nto Government agencies or in the open market as is advantageous to the\nm.\n \n \n \nIn addition, Government has taken several steps to ensure \nMSP for all agricultural \nproduce which inter alia includes setting up of procurement centre keeping in view the potential \nin the areas; creating awareness among the farmers of the MSP operation\ns; making payment \nthrough arthias/co\n-\noperative socie\nties to the farmers through Ac payee cheque/electronic mode \nas per prevailing situation in the states;  encouraging decentralized procurement; adopting e\n-\nprocurement system; engaging private players in ce\nrtain States to participate in procurement \noperation\n \netc.\n \n \n \n \nTo ensure rem\nunerative price to farmers, the Government procured 38.65 million tonnes \nof Rice, 22.93 million tonnes of Wheat and 1.3 million tonnes of pulses during 2016\n-\n17 across \nvarious States.\n \n \n \nGovernment has also launched a scheme developing a pan India electronic\n \ntrading \nplatform under ‘National Agriculture Market’ (NAM) aiming to integrate 585 regulated markets \nwith the common e\n-\nmarket platform to ensure remunerative prices to the farmers.  Each State is \nbeing encouraged to undertake three major reforms \n–\n \nallow \ne\nlectronic trading, have a single \nlicense valid throughout the State and a single entry point market fee.  455 markets in 13 States \nhave already been brought on the e\n-\nNAM platform.\n \n \n \n*******\n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_277": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 277 \nANSWERED ON 03RD AUGUST, 2017 \n \nFOREIGN INVESTMENT IN ROAD PROJECTS \n \n*277.  ADV. M.  UDHAYA KUMAR:  \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n�����������������������������������������������������\nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is formulating a model pact for its projects to suit the need of \nprivate investors, especially from the U.S., the Middle East and Singapore, who have shown \nkeen interest in operating them; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether it is also true that investors from abroad have shown keen interest to buy some of the \nroad projects; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n(a)  to (d)  A STATEMENT is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 277 ANSWERED ON 03 RD AUGUST, 2017 ASKED BY ADV. \nM. UDHAYA KUMAR ����������������������FOREIGN INVESTMENT IN ROAD PROJECTS�� \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \n \n(a) No Madam. No model pact is being formulated for projects to suit the need of private \ninvestors, especially from the U.S., the Middle East and Singapore. \n \n(b) Question does not arise.  \n \n(c) Yes Madam. Monetization of public funded, operational NH projects through the Toll ��\nOperate ��Transfer (ToT) model has been approved by the CCEA. 75 public funded NH projects \nwith aggregate length of 4,500 km and annual toll revenue collection of around Rs 2,700 crores \nhave been identified under the model. Preparatory activities including finalization of the Mo del \nConcession Agreement and RFP document have been completed and the transaction advisor has \nbeen identified. The first round of bidding for ToT projects is to be held shortly. While finalizing \nthe model, adequate stakeholder consultation has been done. I nvestors from abroad have shown \nkeen interest in this model. \n \n(d) Stakeholder workshops on the ToT model have been organized in places like Mumbai, \nDubai and Singapore in which investors like Abu Dhabi Investment Authority (ADIA), Hastings \nInfrastructure, GIC, Keppel Infrastructure Fund Management, Temasek, Mizuho Asia Infra \nCapital, Macquarie, Morgan Stanley Infrastructure, Equirus Capital, I Squared Capital, \nJ.P.Morgan Asset Management, IL&FS and others have showed inte rest to invest in ToT \nprojects. \n*****    \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_278": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †278 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 18TH JULY,  2017 / ASHADHA 27, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nHARASSMENT CASES IN DELHI POLICE \n \n†278. SHRI RAJESH VERMA: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:    \n \n(a) the total number of cases of harassment of subordinate officers/ \npersonnel by the senior officers of Delhi Police reported during each of the \nlast three years and the current year;  \n \n(b) whether the Government has conducted any investigation in this regard \nthrough any committee of senior officials of the Ministry; and  \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the action taken against guilty during the \nsaid period? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n(a) to (c) : As reported by Delhi Police, a  total number of 17 complaints of \nharassment of subordinate officers/personnel by senior officers of Delhi \nPolice during the last three years and the current ye ar (upto 30.06.2017) \nwere received.  The Delhi Police conducts initial enquiry into such \ncomplaints.  During such enquiry, out of these 17 complaints, allegations \nwere not substantiated in 15 complaints. Year -wise details of number of \ncomplaints received, number of complaints substantiated/not substantiated \nand action taken on the substantiated complaints are as under:  \n--2-- \n \n\n \n \n--2— \nL.S.US.Q.NO.278 FOR 18.07.2017 \n \nYear Total \nNumber of \nComplaints \nSubstantiated Not \nSubstantiated \nAction Taken  on the \nsubstantiated complaints \n2014 3 - 3 - \n2015 3 - 3 - \n2016 9 1 8 A Departmental Enquiry  has \nbeen initiated  by Delhi \nPolice against the alleged \nofficer. \n2017 \n(upto \n30.06.17) \n2 1 1 An enquiry has been \nconducted by Delhi Police  \nagainst the alleged officer \nand s ubsequently the \nofficer has been placed \nunder suspension vide  \norder dated 11.05.2017  of \nMinistry of Home Affairs.  \n \n****** ",
