    "ls|LS16_S12_U_305": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n305\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n8\nTH\n  \nAUGUST, 2017\n \n \n \nCROP INSURANCE SCHEME\n \n \n*305. \n   \nSHRIMATI HEMA MALINI: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE   \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \n½ãâ¨ããè\n  \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a)\n \n \nthe details of the public and private sector companies which are empanelled for \ncrop insurance scheme in the country; \n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether it is a fact that the percentage share of Agriculture Insurance Company of \nIndia Limited (AIC) vis\n-\na\n-\nvis private companies in the crop insurance scheme has \ndecreased considerably during each of the last three years and the current year; and\n \n \n(c) \n \ni\nf so, the details thereof along with the number of farmers benefited under the said \nscheme during the said period, State\n-\nwise?\n \n \n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n  \n½ãâ¨ããè\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI RADHA MOHAN SINGH\n)\n \n \n \n(a) to (\nc\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\nc\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n305 DUE\n \nFOR REPLY \nON\n \n8\nTH\n \n  \nAUGUST, 2017\n.\n \n(a):\n \nTotal 18 general insurance companies including all the 5 public sector companies \nand 13 Private Sector \ngeneral insurance\n \ncompanies are presently empanelled for \nimplementation of Crop Insurance Schemes in the country.\n  \n \nDetails are given at \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n.\n \n(b)\n \n& (C)\n:\n \nIn 2014\n-\n15 and 2015\n-\n16 Agriculture Insurance Company of India Ltd. \n(AIC) was the only public sector insurance company which along with 10 private \ninsurance companies implemented the then Government sponsored crop insurance \nschemes and share  of AIC \n(Government insurance company) in terms of sum insured \nwas 75.69% and 80.20% respectively.  In 2016\n-\n17 all the 5 Public Sector Insurance \nCompanies including AIC participated apart from 11 private insurance companies in \nimplementation of the Crop Insurance \nSchemes.  Percentage share of all the Public \nSector Insurance Companies including AIC was 48.33% (out of this AIC’s share was \n38.309% of the total sum insured).  Details are at \nAnnexure\n-\nII.\n \n \nState\n-\nwise details of number of farmers benefitted in terms of cl\naims paid under \nthe crop insurance schemes during the stated period is at \nAnnexure\n-\nIII.\n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nDetails of Empanelled General Insurance Companies for implementation \nof Government sponsored \nCrop Insurance \nschemes\n \n \nPUBLIC SECTOR INSURANCE COMPANIES\n \n1\n \nAGRICULTURE INSUR\nA\nNCE COMPANY OF INDIA LTD.\n \n2\n \nNEW INDIA ASSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n3\n \nNATIONAL INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n4\n \nORIENTAL INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n5\n \nUNITED INDIA INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \nPRIVATE SECTOR INSURANCE COMPANIES\n \n1\n \nBAJAJ ALLIANZ GENERAL \nINSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n2\n \n \nBHARTI AXA GENERAL INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n3\n \nCHOLAMANDALAM MS GENERAL INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n4\n \nFUTURE GENERALI INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n5\n \nHDFC ERGO GENERAL INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n6\n \nICICI LOMBARD GENERAL INSURANCE CO. LTD.\n \n7\n \nIFFCO\n-\nTOKIO GENERAL INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n8\n \nRELIANCE GENERAL INSURANCE COMPANY LIMITED\n \n9\n \nSBI GENERAL INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n10\n \nSHRIRAM GENERAL INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n11\n \nTATA AIG GENERAL INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n12\n \nUNIVERSAL SOMPO GENERAL INSURANCE \nCOMPANY LTD.\n \n13\n \nROYAL SUNDARAM GENERAL INSURANCE COMPANY LTD.\n \n \n \n\nAnnexure \n–\n \nII\n \nPercentage share of implementing insurance companies in total sum insured \n \n(Rs. In crores)\n \nYear\n \nCrop \nInsurance \nSchemes\n \nImplementing \nInsurance \nCompanies\n \nTotal Sum \nInsured\n \nSum \nInsured by AIC & \nother Public Sector \nInsurance Companies\n \nSum Insured \nby Private \nCompanies\n \n2014\n-\n15\n \nNAIS, MNAIS, \nWBCIS & \nCPIS\n \nAIC and 10 \nPrivate \nInsurance \nCompanies \n \n82042\n \n62100\n \n(75.69%)\n \nOnly AIC\n \n19942\n \n(24.31%)\n \n2015\n-\n16\n \n-\n \nDo \n-\n \n-\n \nDo \n-\n \n115085\n \n92291\n \n(80.20%)\n \nOnly \nAIC\n \n22794\n \n(19.80%)\n \n2016\n-\n17\n \nPMFBY, \nRWBCIS and \nCPIS\n \nAIC, 4 other \nPublic Sect\nor \nInsurance \nCompanies and \n11 Private  \nInsurance \nCompanies\n \n202822\n \n98011\n \n(48.33%)\n \nAIC (38.30%) & other\n \nPublic Sector Insurance \nCompanies\n \n104811\n \n(51.67%)\n \nNAIS :\n \nNational Agricultural Insurance Scheme \n \nMNAIS : Modified National Agricultural Insurance Scheme \n \nWBCIS : Weather Based Crop Insurance Scheme \n \nCPIS : Coconut Palm Insurance Scheme\n \nPMFBY : Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana\n \nRWBCIS :\n \nRestructured Weather Based Crop Insurance Scheme \n \n \n \n\n              \nAnnexure\n-\nIII\n \n \nState\n-\nwise Number of farmers benefitted in terms of claims paid  during last \nthree years under crop insurance Schemes\n \n \n \n \n \nYear 2014\n-\n15\n \nYear 2015\n-\n16\n \nYear 2016\n-\n17\n \nSr.No.\n \nState / UT\n \nNo. of Farmers \nbenefitted \n \nNo. of \nFarmers \nbenefitted \n \nNo. of Farmers \nbenefitted \n \n1\n \nAndaman & Nicobar\n \n184\n \n158\n \n0\n \n2\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n115390\n \n415588\n \n787671\n \n3\n \nAssam\n \n22203\n \n24425\n \n23370\n \n4\n \nBihar\n \n2500014\n \n1123440\n \n182545\n \n5\n \nChhatisgarh \n \n596577\n \n677382\n \n121483\n \n6\n \nGoa\n \n0\n \n82\n \n111\n \n7\n \nGujarat\n \n191722\n \n363027\n \n125753\n \n8\n \nHaryana\n \n7\n \n0\n \n150181\n \n9\n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \n89448\n \n92096\n \n27410\n \n10\n \nJammu & Kashmir\n \n1364\n \n0\n \n0\n \n