    "ls|LS16_S12_U_306": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *306 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 08, AUGUST, 2017 / SHRAVANA 17, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nKILLING OF SECURITY PERSONNEL \n \n*306.  SHRI JAYADEV GALLA: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the incidents of killing of  security personnel by terrorists/ISI/  \nPakistan military have risen over the years; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof including  the number of security personnel \nkilled in Jammu and Kashmir (J&K) during each of  the last three years and \nthe current year; \n \n(c) the number of terrorists arrested/ killed during the above period; \n \n(d) whether the Government has taken  note of the consistent spread of \nISIS/ISI in the country and the threat posed to India's  sovereignty and if so,  \nthe details thereof; and \n \n(e) the measures taken by the Government to address the issue? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n-2- \nL.S.S.Q. No. *306 for 08.08.2017 \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *306   FOR \n08TH AUGUST, 2017. \n \n(a) to (c) : The details of casualties of security personnel in the terrorist  \nincidents carried out by Pakistan based/ supported terror groups,  terrorists \narrested/killed in the Jammu & Kashmir and the hinterland of the country \nand security personnel killed in ceasefire violations by Pakistan during each \nof the last three years and the current year are at Annexure. \n(d) & (e) : The Islamic State (IS)/ Islamic State of Iraq and Levant (ISIL)/ \nIslamic State of Iraq and Syria (ISIS)/ Daesh has been notified as a Terrorist \nOrganization and included in the First Schedule to the Unlawful Activities \n(Prevention) Act, 1967 by the Central Government.  ISIS is using various \ninternet based social media platforms to propagate its ideology.  However, \nvery few individuals have come to notice of the Central and State Security \nAgencies who have join ed ISIS.  The National Investigation Agency (NIA) \nand the States Police have also registered cases against ISIS/ISIL \nsympathizers and have arrested around 90 accused so far.  Further, t he \nCentral and State agencies are monitoring the cyber space and taking  \naction as per law wherever required.  In order to assess and counter the \nincipient threat posed by ISIS/ISIL, meetings have been held by the Ministry \nof Home Affairs with the Central agencies and the State Governments  \nconcerned.   \n******* \n\n \n-3- \nL.S.S.Q. No. *306 for 08.08.2017 \n \n \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Starred Question \nNo. *306 for 08.08.2017 \n \n(1)   Hinterland of the country \nYear No. of terror \nincidents \nNumber of security \npersonnel killed \nNumber of \nterrorists killed \nNumber of \nterrorists \narrested \n2014 Nil  Nil Nil Nil \n2015 01(Terror attack in \nGurdaspur District \nof Punjab)  \n04 03 Nil \n2016 01 (Terror attack in \nthe Pathankot \nDistrict of Punjab) \n07 04 Nil \n2017  Nil  Nil Nil Nil \n \n(2)  Jammu & Kashmir \n \nYear No. of terror \nincidents \nNumber of security \npersonnel killed \nNumber of \nterrorists \nkilled \nNumber of \nterrorists \narrested \n2014 222 47 110 70 \n2015 208 39 108 67 \n2016 322 82 150 79 \n2017 ( up to \n31st July) \n194  39 115 44 \n \n(3)  Casualties suffered by the security personnel in ceasefire violations by \nPakistan  \nYear Number of security personnel killed \n2014 03 \n2015 10 \n2016 13 \n2017 ( up to 11th July) 05 \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_307": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALSS & FERTILIZERS \nDEPARTMENT OF CHEMICALS & PETROCHEMICALS \n \nLOK SABHA \nADMITTED STARRED QUESTION NO. 307 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 08.08.2017 \n \nCrop Protection Chemicals \n \n*307: SHRI ANANTKUMAR HEGDE \n \n Will the Minister of Chemicals & Fertilizers be pleased to state:- \n   \n(a) Whether the production and business of crop protection chemicals have constantly \nincreased over the last several years; \n(b) If so, the average annual production and amount of business transacted respect of the said \nchemicals during the last four years; \n (c) Whether the selling price of these chemicals has increased during the said period; and  \n(d) If so, the extent to which the selling price of these chemicals has increased from 2013 -\n2014 to March, 2016-2017. \n                                                              ANSWER \nMINISTER OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS, PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS    \n(SHRI ANANT KUMAR) \n(a) Yes Sir. There has been significant increase in production of crop protection chemicals. \nThe details of  last four years are as under:- \n \nSr. No Year Production (Technical grade) in               \nMetric Ton \n% increase \n01   2013-14 179379 15.41 \n02 2014-15 186466 3.95 \n03 2015-16 187522 0.56 \n04 2016-17 213718 13.96 \n \n(b) The average annual production of crop protection chemicals during last 04 years is 191771 \nMetric Ton.  \n \nContinue.. \n\n \n \n(C)& (d): Department of Chemicals and Petrochemicals does not monitor the selling price of \nCrop protection chemicals. However the wholesale price index of Insecticide and Pesticide \nis being maintained by Office of the Economic Advisor, Department of Industrial  Policy \nand Promotion, Ministry of Commerce and Industry. Based on data published by DIPP on \ntheir website the wholesale price index of insecticides and Pesticides over past four years \nis given below. \n \nBase Year: 2011-12 = 100  \nFinancial Year Index \n2016-17 112.6 \n2015-16 120 \n2014-15 119.1 \n2013-14 109.6 \n2012-13 106.9 \n \n \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_308": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*308 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 08, AUGUST, 2017 / SHRAVANA 17, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nCRIMES BY JUVENILES \n \n†*308.  SHRI RAJAN VICHARE: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the tendency to commit  crimes by juvenile students is on the \nrise in the National Capital Territory (NCT) of Delhi; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with  the number of such cases reported \nand the action taken against the guilty during the last one year, crime -wise \nincluding rape or sexual exploitation of minor girls; and \n \n(c) the steps taken by the Government  to control the crimes by juvenile \nstudents? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n \n(a) to (c):   A statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n--2-- \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO THE LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *308 FOR \n08.08.2017 \n(a) and (b):  Delhi Police has reported that data regarding crime by juvenile \nstudents is not collated separately. However, the number of cases \nregistered by Delhi Police in which juveniles were involved during the \nyears 2015 and 201 6 is 2366 and 2499 respectively.  Crime-wise number of \ncases registered during the last one year is as under: \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nTotal number of juveniles apprehended during 2016 is 3808.  Whenever any \njuvenile in conflict with law is apprehended by police in any criminal case, \nthe juvenile is produced before the Juvenile Justice Board (JJB) within 24 \nhours and the Juvenile Justice Board either releases the juvenile on bail or \nremands him/her to Observation Home depending upon the gravity of \noffence. \n--3-- \n \n \nCrime heads 2016 \nDacoity 10 \nMurder 56 \nAttempt to murder 83 \nRobbery 382 \nRiot 7 \nRape 155 \nGrevious hurt 27 \nBurglary 178 \nMotor vehicle theft 286 \nOther theft cases 497 \nOther IPC cases 771 \nTotal IPC cases 2452 \nTotal Act cases 47 \nGrand total 2499 \n\n \n--3— \nL.S.S.Q.NO. *308 FOR 08.08.2017 \n(c):  As a preventive strategy to control crimes by juveniles, Delhi Police \nhas started the scheme, ‘Yuva’, for young adults and street children of the \nSociety. Under this scheme, workshops, sports activities and vocational \ntrainings etc. are being organized to channelize the energy of young adults \nand children to mak e them productive members of the society and prevent \nthem from moving towards crime and drugs at an early age. Police \npersonnel are also detailed in plainclothes as well as in uniform in and \naround the educational institutions, busy markets, bus stops and other \nvulnerable places to prevent crimes. \n******* \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_309": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  *309 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 08.08.2017 \n \nNATIONAL COMMISSION FOR SCs  \n \n*309. SHRI E.T. MOHAMMED BASHEER:  \n \nWill the Minister of SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT be pleased to state:   \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to take legal a nd administrative measures to strengthen \nthe existing National Commission for Scheduled Castes (NCSC);  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) the steps taken/being taken by the Government in this regard? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT \n(SHRI THAAWARCHAND GEHLOT) \n \n(a): The National Commission for Scheduled Castes ( NCSC) is a Constitutional Body set up \nunder Article 338 of the Constitution.  The Commiss ion has powers to investigate and \nmonitor all matters relating to safeguards provided  to the Scheduled Castes, to inquire into \nspecific complaints with respect to deprivation of rights etc.  The new Chairman, Vice-\nChairman and three members have assumed the office in the Commission in June, 2017.  The \nCommission is functioning with 12 Regional Offices and discharging its duties satisfactorily. \nThe Government would take necessary action to stren gthen the Commission as and when \nrequired. \n \n(b) & (c): Does not arise. \n \n***** \n \n \n ",
