    "ls|LS16_S12_U_384": "ORIGINAL IN HINDI \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 384 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18TH July, 2017 \n \nFOODGRAIN RELEASED TO MAHARASHTRA \n \n384.  SHRIMATI BHAVANA PUNDALIKRAO GAWALI PATIL: \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC \nDISTRIBUTION miHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h   be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the quantum of rice and wheat  released to the State of Maharashtra  \nthrough Public Distribution System under  BPL, APL and AAY during the last \nthree years; \n \n(b)  the details of the wheat and rice released under the General scheme \nand  adhoc scheme;  \n \n(c)  whether the State of Maharashtra has not been released the share to \nbe allotted by the Union Government under the ad-hoc scheme since July, \n2016 and if so, the reasons therefor; and  \n \n(d)  whether the Union Government is  ready to release the share for this \nperiod and if so, the details thereof? \n \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR  CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI C. R. CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a) & (b):   Government of Maharashtra implemented the National Food \nSecurity Act (NFSA) from February, 2014 .  So, while protecting the annual \naverage offtake of 3 years preceding the year when NFSA came into effect, \nfollowing allocation of foodgrain was made to Maharashtra during last \nthree years: \n                                                         (in thousand tons) \nYear Wheat Rice Total \n2014-15 1986.999 2540.493 4527.492 \n2015-16 2021.100 2584.092 4605.192 \n2016-17 2021.100 2584.092 4605.192 \n \n(c) & (d): Maharashtra has already implemented NFSA and as per the Act, \nno \nad hoc allocation is provided to NFSA implementing States/UTs.  \n***  \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_385": " \nORIGINAL IN HINDI \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 385 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18TH JULY, 2017 \n \nSUGAR UNDER PDS \n \n385.  DR. VIRENDRA KUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC \nDISTRIBUTION miHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h   be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the State -wise details of the allocation and offtake of sugar under  \nPublic Distribution System during each of the last three years and the current \nyear; \n \n(b)  whether some States have not been able to offtake the quota of \nallocated sugar during the said period; and  \n \n(c)  if so, the details thereof along with the names of the States and the \nreasons therefor? \n \n \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR  CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI C. R. CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a): The mill/state-wise allocation and offtake based system for distribution \nof sugar through Public Distribution System (PDS) was dismantled in April, 2013 \nwith the de- regulation of sugar sector and removal of levy obligation on sugar \nmills. A new dispensation was put in place with effect from 1.6.2013 wherein \nStates/UTs were required to procure sugar from open market for meeting their \nPDS requirement and the Central Government was to reimburse a fixed subsidy \nto the participating States/UTs @ Rs. 18.50 per kg for the quantity of sugar so \ndistributed by them; limited to their fixed quota for the targeted population. \nThe Central Government has further, reviewed the sugar subsidy scheme and \nrestricted its coverage to Antyodaya Anna Yojana (AAY) families with effect \nfrom 01.06.2017. \n \n(b) & (c): Do not arise. \n \n**** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_386": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 386. \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 18TH JULY, 2017/ ASHADHA 27, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nINFILTRATION ATTEMPTS ALONG LOC \n \n386.  SHRI NINONG ERING: \n  SHRI JYOTIRADITYA M. SCINDIA \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware  that in the past few months there \nwas a  spurt in infiltration attempts across the  Line of Control in Jammu \nand Kashmir; \n \n(b) if so, the details in this regard; \n \n(c) whether a portion of border fencing  have been cut by terrorists in  \nJammu and Kashmir and they sneaked in from that portion; \n \n(d) if so, whether the security forces  have launched combing operations \nalong the border belt; and \n \n(e) if so, the plans formulat ed by the  Union Government to nab such  \nterrorists and to strengthen its forces along the borders? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) & (b): The details of infiltration attempts during the past six months \nand corresponding period of last year are as follows : \nMonth Number of Infiltration attempts \n 2016 2017 \nJanuary 02 07 \nFebruary 01 04 \nMarch 02 04 \nApril 02 06 \nMay 05 11 \nJune 07 10 \n...2/ \n \n\n \n-2- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.386 FOR 18.7.2017 \n \n \n(c) : A few incidents have been reported by field formation, wherein \nterrorists have attempted infiltration by cutting the Anti Infiltration \nObstacle System (AIOS) i.e. LC fence However, even if the AIOS is \nbreached, \n the multi-tiered deployment is generally able to detect the breach and \ncombing operations are launched immediately with an aim to neutralize \nthe terrorists. \n \n(d) & (e): In J&K along the Line of Control, the Army has adopted a \nrobust counter infiltration st rategy which is an appropriate mix of \ntechnology and human resources put together to check infiltration. \nInnovative troop deployment in tiers ahead of the AIOS and in hinterland \nconcurrent with efficient use of surveillance and monitoring devices \nhave enhanced the ability to detect and intercept terrorists attempting \nto infiltrate/exfiltrate. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_387": " \n                                       \n  \n                       \n          \n                             \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUEST\nION NO.\n3\n87\n \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n1\n8\nTH\n \nJULY\n, \n201\n7\n \n \nCONVERSION OF RKVY INTO RAFTAAR\n \n \n387.\n \n \nSHRI A.T. NANA PATIL:\n \n \nSHRI RAOSAHEB DANVE\n \nPATIL:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n   \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \n \nwhether the Government proposes\n \nto revamp the existing Rashtriya Krishi\n \nVikas Yojana \ninto RKVY\n-\nRaftaar;\n \n \n(b)\n \n \nif so, the details thereof; and\n \n \n(c)\n \n \nthe steps taken by the Government\n \nfor development of\n \nagriculture\n \ninfrastructure \nspecifically post\n-\nharvest\n \ninfrastructure and promotion of private\n \ninvestment in agriculture across \nthe country\n \nin a big way?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\n\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य मं\u0000ी\n \n \n   \n(\nSHRI  \nPARSHOTTAM RUPALA\n)\n \n \n(a) to (c):\n \nYes, Madam.  The Rashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana is proposed to be revamped as \nRashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana \n–\n \nRemunerative Approaches for Agriculture and Allied sector \nRejuvenation (RKVY \n–\n \nR\nAFTAAR) with the objective of making  the farming as a remunerative  \neconomic  activity through strengthening the farmer’s effort, risk mitigation\n \nand promoting agri\n-\nbusiness entrepreneurship.  The proposed  revamped  scheme provides focus on development \no\nf agricultural infrastructure  including post harvest  infrastructure and promotion of private \ninvestment in agriculture across the country.\n \n \n \n******** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_388": " \n                                       \n  \n                       \n          \n                             \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUEST\nION NO.\n3\n88\n \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n1\n8\nTH\n \nJULY\n, \n201\n7\n \n \nPROCUREMENT OF AGRICULTURAL PRODUCE AT MSP\n \n \n388. \n \nSHRI M.B. RAJESH:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n   \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nth\ne details of the procurement of \nagricultu\nral produce by Food Corporation \nof India \n(FCI) \nand National Agricultural \nCooperative Marketing Federation of India (\nNAFED) at Minimum \nSupport Price \n(MSP) dur\ning the last three years;\n \n \n(b)\n \n \nthe \nnumber of agricultural products \ncovered under the Minimum Supp\nort Price \n(MSP);\n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government proposes\n \nto \nensure MSP at 50% more than the \ncomprehensive \nproduction costs\n \nestablished by CACP, if so, the detai\nls\n \nthereof;\n \n \n(d)\n \n \nwhether the Government proposes \nto pass the leg\nislation to protect the farmers \nright to \nsel\nl their produce at MSP and also \nto ensur\ne an annual automatic review of \nMSP; and\n \n \n(e)\n \n \nif so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN TH\nE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य मं\u0000ी\n \n \n   \n(\nSHRI  \nPARSHOTTAM RUPALA\n)\n \n \n(a):\n \n \nT\nhe details of the procurement of agricultural produce by Food Corporation of India (FCI) \nand National Agricultural Cooperat\nive Marketing Federation of India (NAFED) at Minimum \nSupport Price (MSP) during the last three years are placed at Annexure\n-\nI and Annexure\n-\nII \nrespectively. \n \n \n(b):\n \n \nThere are 25 agricultural products which are covered under the Minimum Support Price \n(MSP).\n \n \n(c):\n \n \nThe National Commission on Farmers under the Chairmanship of Prof. M.S. \nSwaminathan had recommended that the MSP should be at least 50% more than the weighted \naverage cost\ns\n \nof production. MSP is recommended by the CACP based on various factors \ninclu\nding cost of cultivation.  The CACP also includes a certain profit margin on the A2+FL \n(family labour) cost.  A2 cost includes all paid out costs.  Government considers the MSP \nrecommended by CACP and notifies the same.\n \n \n \nContd\n…2/\n-\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \nAs regards r\necommendation of National Commission on Farmers (NCF) to fix 50% as \nprofit margin on C2 cost, the Department has shared certain issues with M.S. Swaminathan \nResearch Foundation (MSSRF), and sought for comments.\n \n \n(d) & (e):\n \n \nMSP is notified by the Governmen\nt on various Kharif and Rabi crops.  \nGovernment’s aim is to help farmers realise prices higher than MSP in the market.  For this \npurpose, Government has been focussing on creating an efficient marketing system.  Towards \nthis, the Government has shared a Mo\ndel Agricultural Produce and Livestock Marketing \n(Promotion & Fa\ncilitation) Act, 2017 with the S\ntates & UTs.  This will encourage more number of \nmarkets and enhance competition.  The Government is also aiming at creating a unified \nNational Agriculture Mark\net (eNAM) by promoting market integration through online trade.\n \n \nHowever, there can still be situations where prices in the market rule below MSP.  This is \naddressed through the instrument of Price Support Scheme (PSS) and Market Intervention \nScheme (MIS).\n  \nUnder these schemes\n,\n \nprocurement is undertaken based on the requests of the \nState Governments.  While PSS covers non\n-\nperishable commodities like pulses & oilseeds, MIS \ncovers perishables.\n \n \n \n\n \n \nAnnexure \n-\n \nI\n \n \n