    "ls|LS16_S12_U_389": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 389. \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 18TH JULY, 2017/ ASHADHA 27, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nINTERNATIONAL CENTRE OF EXCELLENCE IN INVESTIGATION \n \n389.  SHRI B. VINOD KUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether there is any proposal for  setting up of International Centre of  \nExcellence in Investigation (ICEI -CBI) and  International Centre of  \nExcellence in Forensic Science; \n \n(b) if so, the details of schemes  undertaken to improve its functioning and  \nto make it a premier investigative agency; and \n \n(c) the details of cases pending under  investigation for more than three \nyears, including the current year? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) & (b) The proposal for setting up of International Centre of Excellence \nin Investigation (ICE-CBI) is under review.  In addition to this, the following \nprojects are also being undertaken by CBI to improve its efficiency : \n \ni) E-Governance - This is a Rs.48.63 Crore project, envisaging \nautomation of all the current processes of the CBI.  It aims at removin g \nduplicity in investigation and usher in enhanced supervision of all the \nprocesses in CBI by use of technology.  The project also encompasses \ndigitization  of  4.82 crore documents in CBI.  The project is expected to go  \n..2/ \n\n \n-2- \nR.S.US.Q.NO.389 FOR 18.7.2017 \n \nlive in the current financial year.  Once implemented, the project is likely \nto give a giant leap to CBI in so far as ushering efficiency in its functioning \nis concerned.  The project is at an advanced stage of implementation. \n \nii) CTV-CBI -    This is a Rs.100 Crore project through which CBI intends \nto set up a Centralized Technology Vertical (CTV), State of Art Technology \nCentre and build in House Central Capacity for supporting specialized \ncrime investigations dealing with Digital Forensic Analysis, Forensic \nAccounting, Fraud Analytics and Big Data Analysis.   \n \niii) Training of CBI officers at IIM Bangalore and  NLSUI Bangalore  - \nTraining of CBI officers at IIM Bangalore and NLSUI Bangalore is being \nundertaken by CBI Academy for Advanced Certified Courses on Financial \nCrime Investigation and Advanced Certified Courses of Cyber Crimes \nInvestigation & Cyber Laws. These courses are  being conducted under \nScheme of Comprehensive Modernization of CBI Branches and Offices.    \nAlready four batches of 100 CBI officers have been trained in NLSUI \nBangalore and 60 Officers at IIM Bangalore.  These courses are expected \nto continue for the next five years also. \n \n(c)  As on 30.06.2017, 88 Regular Cases (RCs) and 7 Preliminary Enquiries \n(PEs) were pending investigation/enquiry for more than three years. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S12_U_390": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 390. \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 18TH JULY, 2017/ ASHADHA 27, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nCRIME AGAINST WOMEN AND CHILDREN \n \n390.  SHRI P.K. BIJU: \nSHRI NISHIKANT DUBEY: \nSHRI P. KARUNAKARAN: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the details of cases of crimes  against girls, children and women  \nreported during the last one year in the country; \n \n(b) whether it is a fact that crimes  against children and women in the  \ncountry are on the rise; and \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the corrective steps taken thereon? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n \n(a) & (b): State/UT-wise cases registered under crimes against children \nand women is enclosed as Annexure-I & II.  \n(c): As per the Seventh Schedule to the Constitution of India, “Police” and \n“Public Order” are State subjects and, as such the primary responsibility of  \nprevention, detection, registration, investigation and prosecution of crime \nlies with the States/UT Administrations.  \nMinistry  of  Home  Affairs  has  issued advisories on 04.09.2009, 14.7.2010,  \n...2/ \n\n \n-2- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.390 FOR 18.7.2017 \n \n5.1.2015, 20.4.2015 and 12.05.2015 on Crime against women and crime \nagainst children, to all State Governments/UTs. These advisories \nspecifically direct the States/UTs that cases should be thoroughly \ninvestigated and chargesheets against the accused persons should be filed \nwithin three months from the date of occurrence, without compromising on \nthe quality of investigation. Speedy investigation should be conducted in \nheinous crimes like rape, murder etc. The medical examination of rape \nvictims should be conducted wit hout delay. These advisories are available \nat www.mha.nic.in.  \n**** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nANNEXURE-I \nL.S.US.Q.NO.390 FOR 18.7.2017 \nState/UT-wise cases registered under crime against children during 2014-2016* \nSl. \nNo. State/UT 2014 2015 2016* \n1 Andhra Pradesh 2059 1992 1908 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 134 181 133 \n3 Assam 1385 2835 2978 \n4 Bihar 2255 1917 3932 \n5 Chhattisgarh 4358 4469 4746 \n6 Goa 330 242 230 \n7 Gujarat 3219 3623 3604 \n8 Haryana 2540 3262 3099 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 467 477 467 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir 211 308 222 \n11 Jharkhand 423 406 581 \n12 Karnataka 3416 3961 4455 \n13 Kerala 2391 2384 2881 \n14 Madhya Pradesh 15085 12859 13746 \n15 Maharashtra 8115 13921 14559 \n16 Manipur 137 110 133 \n17 Meghalaya 213 257 242 \n18 Mizoram 178 186 188 \n19 Nagaland 25 61 78 \n20 Odisha 2196 2562 3286 \n21 Punjab 1762 1836 1843 \n22 Rajasthan 3880 3689 4034 \n23 Sikkim 93 64 110 \n24 Tamil Nadu 2354 2617 2856 \n25 Telangana 1930 2697 2913 \n26 Tripura 369 255 274 \n27 Uttar Pradesh 14835 11420 NR \n28 Uttarakhand 489 635 676 \n29 West Bengal 4909 4963 NR \n  TOTAL STATE(S) 79758 84189 74174 \n30 A & N Islands 50 102 78 \n31 Chandigarh 208 271 222 \n32 D&N Haveli 11 35 21 \n33 Daman & Diu 7 28 31 \n34 Delhi UT 9350 9489 8108 \n35 Lakshadweep 1 2 5 \n36 Puducherry 38 56 71 \n  TOTAL UT(S) 9665 9983 8536 \n  TOTAL (ALL INDIA) 89423 94172 82710 \nSource: Crime in India \n   Note:  * Data for the year 2016 is provisional. \n  Note:  NR implies data not received from the State of Uttar Pradesh and West Bengal. \n \n \n \n \n\n \nANNEXURE-II \nL.S.US.Q.NO.390 FOR 18.7.2017 \n \nState/UT-wise cases registered under crime against women during 2014-2016* \nSl. \nNo. State/UT 2014 2015 2016* \n1 Andhra Pradesh 16558 15997 16853 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 352 384 428 \n3 Assam 19472 24664 23189 \n4 Bihar 15675 14208 13619 \n5 Chhattisgarh 6298 5769 6521 \n6 Goa 502 391 370 \n7 Gujarat 10845 7770 8858 \n8 Haryana 9276 9674 10846 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 1525 1291 1290 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir 3322 3364 2854 \n11 Jharkhand 6103 6596 5794 \n12 Karnataka 13993 12786 14250 \n13 Kerala 11394 9723 11167 \n14 Madh