    "ls|LS16_S12_U_403": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n403\n                     \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE  \n1\n8\nTH\n \nJULY\n, 2017\n \n \n       \n    \nMSP FOR PULSES, \nOILSEEDS AND COTTON\n \n \n403. \n \nSHRI MOHITE PATIL\n \nVIJAYSINH\n \nSHANKARRAO:\n \nSHRI P.R. SUNDARAM:\n \nDR. J. JAYAVARDHAN:\n \nSHRI C.N. JAYADEVAN:\n \nDR. HEENA\n \nVIJAYKUMAR GAVIT:\n \nADV. NARENDRA KESHAV\n \nSAWAIKAR:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n  \n‡ãðŠãäÓã \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \n½ãâ¨ããè\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n \n(a) \n \nthe details of the estimated\n \nproduction of pulses, cotton and oilseeds\n \nduring each \nof the last three years and the\n \ncurrent year;\n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether it is a fact that\n \nfarmers from various parts of the country\n \nhave been \n \ndemanding increase in the\n \nMinimum Support Price (MSP)\n \nfor oilseeds, cotton and \npulses, if so, the\n \ndetails thereof along with the\n \nresponse of the Government\n \nthereto;\n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Commission for\n \nAgricultural Costs and Prices (CACP) has\n \nalso \nr\necommended for increase in MSP for\n \npulses, oilseeds and cotton for 2017\n-\n2018\n \ncrop \nyear, if so, the details of the MSP\n \nfixed by the Government for these\n \nitems;\n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether the Government\n \nhas also directed to the States to procure\n \nall farm \nproduce so that \nfarmers are not\n \nforced to sell their produce at lower\n \nprices, if so, the \ndetails thereof;\n \nand\n \n \n(e) \n \nwhether his Ministry had also\n \nmeeting with seed companies to cut prices\n \nof \nhybrid seeds by 10%, if so, the outcome\n \nthereof?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF  STATE\n \nIN THE  MINISTRY OF  AGRICULTURE AND  FARMERS  WELFARE\n \n \n‡ãðŠãäÓã  \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \n½ãâ¨ããÊã¾ã ½ãñâ Àã•¾ã ½ãâ¨ããè          \n \n( SHRI\n \nS.S. \nAHLUWALIA\n)  \n \n \n(a):\n \nThe production of pulses, cotton and oilseeds for the years 2013\n-\n14, 2014\n-\n15, \n2015\n-\n16 and 2016\n-\n17 is \nat \nAnnexure I.\n \n \n  \n\n \nContd…2/\n-\n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \n \n(b) to (d):\n \nRepresentations are received from time to time from various organizations \nrequesting for increase in Minimum Support Prices (MSP) of various crops including \npulses, oilseeds and cotton.\n \n \nGovernment fixes MSP on the recommendations of Commission for Agricultural \nCosts and Prices (CACP), views of State Governments, Central Ministries/Departments \nand other relevant factors. MSPs fixed by the Government for pulses, oilseeds and \ncotton for 2015\n-\n16, 2016\n-\n17 and 2017\n-\n18 are at \nAnnexure\n-\nII.\n \n \nGovernment ensures Minimum Support Price (MSP) through procurement \noperations undertaken by the Central, State and Cooperative agencies in the States. \nState Governments have been alerted from time to time to ma\nke adequate \narrangements to ensure MSP to farmers.\n \n \nMSP is in the nature of minimum price offered by the Government to farmers to \nprocure their produce when market prices tend to fall below MSP. However, farmers are \nfree to sell their produce to Government\n \nagencies or in the open market as is \nadvantageous to them. \n \n(e):\n \nDuring a meeting held on 16.06.2017, representatives of seed companies agreed \nto reduce the selling price (on MRP) of hybrid seeds except cotton seeds by 10 percent \nduring Kharif 2017\n-\n18.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nAnnexure\n–\nI\n \n \n \nStatement referred to in reply to part (a) of \nLok Sabha \nUnstarred Question No. 403 \nfor answer on 18.07.2017 regarding “MSP for pulses, oilseed\ns\n \nand cotton”\n \n \n \nPRODUCTION OF PULSES, OILSEEDS AND COTTON\n \n           \n \n                                                                  