    "ls|LS16_S12_U_474": "O.I.H. \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK  SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 474 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JULY 19, 2017 \n \nBASIC FACILITIES \n \nNo. 474 SHRI RAM CHARAN BOHRA: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSIN G AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)  whether the pro gramme for providing basic facilities and \nintegrated housing for urban poor and constructing housing units \nunder slums development programme is running as per schedule and \nif so, the details thereof; and if not, the reasons therefor;  \n \n(b)  the State-wise and city-wise number of housing units \nconstructed under the above schemes,  year-wise during the last \nthree years;  \n \n(c) whether the Government has received complaints in \nimplementation of above schemes in certain States; and  \n \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and the action taken/being taken by the \nGovernment in this regard?       \n                                          \n                                                ANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOUSING AND \nURBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a)  : Government has launched ‘Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-\nHousing for All (Urban)’ Mission on 25.6.2015 to provide central \nassistance to States/UTs for prov iding housing to all eligible urban \npoor, including slum dwellers. T he mission envisages that houses \nconstructed by the States / UTs should have basic civic infrastructure \nlike water, sanitation, sewerage, road, electricity etc.  \nContd…2/- \n\n \n-2- \n \nThe PMAY (U) scheme guidelines require States/UTs to conduct \ndemand assessment and validate the same to arrive at the actual \ndemand for housing among its citizens belonging to the urban poor.  \n \n \n(b): State and City-w ise details of housing units constructed during \nthe last three years and the current year under PMAY(U) mission are \nat Annexure. \n \n(c) & (d) : Complaints received in connection with the \nimplementation of PMAY(U) mission are sent to State Government \n/Union Territories (UTs) for remedial action as the implementation of  \nprojects are undertaken by the respective State Governments/UTs \nand their implementing agencies, primarily Urban Local Bodies. \n \n ****** \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure referred in answer to LSUSQ No - 474 due for 19.07.2017 \nStates / UTs and City wise details of Houses sanctioned, and Constructed \nby urban poor beneficiaries during last three year and current year under \nPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana - PMAY(Urban) \n \nAs on 10th July 2017 \nMonitoring Division‐ MoHUA\n \n \n \n \nSr. No. \n \nCity Name State Name Houses \nSanctioned \nHouses \nCompleted \n1 Port Blair A&N Island 609 - \n  A&N Island Total  609 - \n2 Atmakur Andhra Pradesh 1,028 - \n3 Nellimarla Andhra Pradesh 325 170 \n4 Palasa Andhra Pradesh 192 100 \n5 Rajam Andhra Pradesh 1 1\n6 Amadalavalasa Andhra Pradesh 512 432 \n7 Srikakulam Andhra Pradesh 1,476 196 \n8 Parvathipuram Andhra Pradesh 836 23 \n9 Bobbili Andhra Pradesh 385 48 \n10 Salur Andhra Pradesh 588 12 \n11 Vizianagaram Andhra Pradesh 9,257 562 \n12 Visakhapatnam Andhra Pradesh 20,262 2,738\n13 Tuni Andhra Pradesh 5,100 29 \n14 Peddapuram Andhra Pradesh 1,724 - \n15 Rajahmundry Andhra Pradesh 4,214 14 \n16 Samalkota Andhra Pradesh 1,048 - \n17 Pithapuram Andhra Pradesh 874 - \n18 Kakinada Andhra Pradesh 4,620 12 \n19 Mandapeta Andhra Pradesh 4,064 - \n20 Ramachandrapuram Andhra Pradesh 1,090 2 \n21 Amalapuram Andhra Pradesh 1,636 - \n22 Tadepalligudem Andhra Pradesh 5,786 53 \n23 Eluru Andhra Pradesh 1,551 13 \n24 Bhimavaram Andhra Pradesh 9,501 1 \n25 Palacole Andhra Pradesh 7,470 52 \n26 Vijaywada Andhra Pradesh 11,443 49\n27 Gudivada Andhra Pradesh 3,317 5 \n28 Pedana Andhra Pradesh 1 1\n29 Machilipatnam Andhra Pradesh 1,851 253 \n30 Tadepalle Andhra Pradesh 1 1\n31 Mangalagiri Andhra Pradesh 2,592 - \n32 Sattenapalli Andhra Pradesh 642 2 \n33 Narasaraopet Andhra Pradesh 1,507 3 \n34 Chil